{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Giving (2nd)","html":"<article id='an8.32'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Aṅguttara Nikāya 8.32 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Numbered Discourses 8.32 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>4. Dānavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>4. Giving </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dutiyadānasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Giving (2nd) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Saddhā hiriyaṁ kusalañca dānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Faith, conscience, and skillful giving </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dhammā ete sappurisānuyātā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are qualities true persons follow. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etañhi maggaṁ diviyaṁ vadanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For this, they say, is the path of the gods, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etena hi gacchati devalokan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>which leads to the heavenly realm.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Dutiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
